# Compactly supported group cohomology and integral modular-symbol evaluations

Definition: `MTT_Cohomology` (`e1071a6e-f650-406b-94af-c5d9a4ff3e07`), by davidloeffler, 2026-09-06.

Define degree-one relative group cohomology as Gamma-equivariant additive divisor-pair functions
with homogeneous binary polynomial values. This is Hom_Gamma(Div^0(P^1(Q)), Sym^n R^2), over an
arbitrary commutative ring. Define the integral coefficient evaluations, coefficientwise extension
and canonical tensor base change, the explicitly normalized prime-Hecke and reflection formulas,
nebentype/sign eigenpackets, and analytic integration comparison predicates. No analytic or
arithmetic theorem is assumed in this definition file. Integral group cohomology is distinguished
from cohomology of the coarse quotient at elliptic stabilizers.

<!-- Generated by add_prove2me_provenance.py -->
